# Lightstall Inquisitor with Archon of Emeria: Bot2 plays the Tundra it exiled. Two replacement effects would make it enter
# tapped - the permission's "each land played this way enters tapped" and Archon's "nonbasic lands your opponents control
# enter tapped" (CR 614.1d) - so Bot2, whose land it is, chooses which applies first (CR 616.1). It picks the permission's;
# Archon's then has nothing left to change (CR 616.1f), and the Tundra is tapped.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Lightstall Inquisitor
Plains
Archon of Emeria
Plains
Plains x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Tundra
Island x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightstall Inquisitor.Cast
Bot2.Choose(Tundra)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Archon of Emeria.Cast
[T6 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Exile.Tundra.Play
Bot2.Replace(played this way)
[T6 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 6
Exile.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 5
Bot2.Battlefield = Tundra
Bot2.Battlefield.Tundra.Tapped = true
